#!markdown

# 08 · Financial NLP

**English.** Markets move on words: earnings releases, guidance, analyst notes, regulatory news. `Finance.NewsAnalytics` turns text into signals with a Loughran-McDonald-style financial lexicon (general-purpose sentiment lists misread words like *liability* or *tax*), entity and ticker extraction, event classification, near-duplicate detection and earnings-call analysis. `Finance.LLM` adds FinGPT-style tasks on any chat model and FinBERT through Hugging Face.

**Bahasa Indonesia.** Pasar bergerak karena kata-kata: rilis laba, panduan (guidance), catatan analis, berita regulasi. `Finance.NewsAnalytics` mengubah teks menjadi sinyal dengan leksikon keuangan bergaya Loughran-McDonald (daftar sentimen umum salah membaca kata seperti *liability* atau *tax*), ekstraksi entitas dan ticker, klasifikasi event, deteksi berita hampir-duplikat, dan analisis earnings call. `Finance.LLM` menambahkan tugas ala FinGPT pada model chat apa pun serta FinBERT melalui Hugging Face.

> Dibuat oleh Gravicode Studios dipimpin oleh Kang Fadhil

#!csharp

#i "nuget: ../artifacts/packages"
#r "nuget: Gravicode.Finance.NewsAnalytics, 0.2.0"
#r "nuget: Gravicode.Finance.LLM, 0.2.0"

using Finance.NewsAnalytics;
using Finance.LLM;

string[] headlines =
{
    "Apple beats earnings expectations as iPhone revenue surges to a record",
    "Tesla shares slump after analysts downgrade the stock on weak delivery guidance",
    "Microsoft announces $60 billion share buyback and raises its quarterly dividend",
    "Regulators open an antitrust investigation into Alphabet's advertising business",
    "Nvidia raises full-year guidance; demand for AI chips remains strong",
    "Amazon faces lawsuit over alleged violations of consumer protection rules",
    "Uncertainty grows as the Fed signals rates may stay higher for longer",
    "Apple beats earnings expectations as iPhone revenue surges to a record.",
};

#!markdown

## Lexicon sentiment / Sentimen leksikon

**EN.** Each headline is tokenised, matched against positive, negative, uncertainty, litigious and constraining word lists, with negation ("not strong") and intensifiers handled. The score is in [-1, 1].

**ID.** Setiap judul berita dipecah menjadi token lalu dicocokkan dengan daftar kata positif, negatif, ketidakpastian, litigasi dan pembatas, dengan penanganan negasi ("not strong") dan penguat. Skornya berada di rentang [-1, 1].

#!csharp

var lexicon = new LexiconSentimentModel();
var extractor = new EntityExtractor();
foreach (var h in headlines)
{
    var s = lexicon.Score(h);
    var tickers = extractor.ExtractTickers(h);
    var events = EventClassifier.Classify(h);
    Console.WriteLine($"{s.Score,6:+0.00;-0.00;0.00} {s.Label,-8} [{string.Join(",", tickers)}] {events}");
    Console.WriteLine($"         {h}");
}

#!markdown

## Near-duplicates / Berita hampir-duplikat

**EN.** Wire stories are re-published with small edits. MinHash signatures over word shingles estimate Jaccard similarity cheaply, so duplicates can be clustered before they double-count in a sentiment index.

**ID.** Berita kantor berita sering diterbitkan ulang dengan sedikit perubahan. Tanda tangan MinHash atas shingle kata memperkirakan kemiripan Jaccard secara murah, sehingga duplikat dapat dikelompokkan sebelum terhitung ganda dalam indeks sentimen.

#!csharp

var detector = new DuplicateDetector();
Console.WriteLine($"Jaccard(first, last) = {detector.Jaccard(headlines[0], headlines[^1]):F2}");
var items = headlines.Select((h, i) => new NewsItem(h, DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.AddMinutes(-i))).ToList();
var clusters = detector.Cluster(items);
Console.WriteLine($"{items.Count} headlines → {clusters.Count} distinct stories");

#!markdown

## Parsing RSS / Membaca RSS

**EN.** `FeedReader` parses RSS 2.0 and Atom. Here we parse an embedded sample; `FeedReader.YahooFinanceUrl("AAPL")` and `GoogleNewsUrl(...)` give live feeds.

**ID.** `FeedReader` membaca RSS 2.0 dan Atom. Di sini kita membaca contoh yang disematkan; `FeedReader.YahooFinanceUrl("AAPL")` dan `GoogleNewsUrl(...)` memberikan feed langsung.

#!csharp

string rss = """
<rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Sample</title>
<item><title>Meta shares jump after strong advertising growth</title><pubDate>Mon, 06 Oct 2025 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><link>https://example.com/1</link></item>
<item><title>Intel cuts outlook amid weak PC demand</title><pubDate>Mon, 06 Oct 2025 14:30:00 GMT</pubDate><link>https://example.com/2</link></item>
</channel></rss>
""";
var parsed = FeedReader.Parse(rss);
var scored = await new NewsIntelligence().ProcessAsync(parsed);
foreach (var n in scored)
    Console.WriteLine($"{n.Item.Published:yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm}  {n.Sentiment.Score:+0.00;-0.00}  [{string.Join(",", n.Item.Tickers)}]  {n.Item.Title}");

#!markdown

## Earnings-call analysis / Analisis earnings call

**EN.** The analyser splits prepared remarks from the Q&A at the operator's hand-off. A drop in tone from scripted remarks to unscripted answers is a classic warning sign.

**ID.** Penganalisis memisahkan sambutan yang sudah disiapkan dari sesi tanya jawab pada saat operator menyerahkan giliran. Penurunan nada dari sambutan tertulis ke jawaban spontan adalah tanda peringatan klasik.

#!csharp

string transcript = """
Prepared remarks. Thank you everyone. We delivered record revenue and strong margin expansion this quarter.
Demand was robust across regions and we expect continued growth next year. We are raising our full-year guidance.
Operator: We will now begin the question-and-answer session.
Analyst: Can you talk about supply constraints? CEO: There is some uncertainty around component availability and we may see delays.
Analyst: What about the pending litigation? CFO: We believe the lawsuit is without merit, but outcomes are difficult to predict.
""";
var call = EarningsCallAnalyzer.Analyze(transcript);
Console.WriteLine($"Prepared remarks tone {call.PreparedRemarks.Score:+0.00;-0.00} | Q&A tone {call.QuestionAndAnswer.Score:+0.00;-0.00} | shift {call.ToneShift:+0.00;-0.00}");
Console.WriteLine($"Uncertainty ratio {call.UncertaintyRatio:P1}; topics: {string.Join(", ", call.TopTopics.Take(5).Select(t => t.Term))}");
foreach (var f in call.ForwardLookingStatements) Console.WriteLine("  FLS: " + f.Trim());

#!markdown

## Optional: LLM and FinBERT / Opsional: LLM dan FinBERT

**EN.** Set `FINANCENET_LLM_KEYFILE` (or `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` + `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT`) to run FinGPT-style tasks; set `FINANCENET_HF_TOKENFILE` for FinBERT. Keys are read at run time and never printed.

**ID.** Atur `FINANCENET_LLM_KEYFILE` (atau `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` + `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT`) untuk menjalankan tugas ala FinGPT; atur `FINANCENET_HF_TOKENFILE` untuk FinBERT. Kunci dibaca saat dijalankan dan tidak pernah dicetak.

#!csharp

// optional-live
try
{
    var settings = LlmSettings.FromEnvironment();
    if (settings is null) Console.WriteLine("No LLM configured — skipping.");
    else
    {
        var tasks = new FinancialTasks(settings.CreateChatModel());
        var sentiment = await tasks.ClassifySentimentAsync(headlines[1]);
        Console.WriteLine($"LLM sentiment: {sentiment.Label} ({sentiment.Score:+0.00;-0.00}) — {sentiment.Rationale}");
        var summary = await tasks.SummarizeHeadlinesAsync(headlines);
        Console.WriteLine($"Summary: {summary.Summary}\nThemes: {string.Join(", ", summary.KeyThemes)}");
    }
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("FINANCENET_HF_TOKENFILE") is { Length: > 0 } tokenFile)
    {
        var finbert = new FinBertSentiment(new HuggingFaceInference(new System.Net.Http.HttpClient(), LlmSettings.ReadHuggingFaceToken(tokenFile)));
        var fb = await finbert.AnalyzeAsync(headlines[0]);
        Console.WriteLine($"FinBERT: {fb.Label} ({fb.Confidence:P0})");
    }
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Live NLP unavailable: {ex.Message}");
}
